WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.667
Voters will have

00:00:00.667 --> 00:00:02.402
to wait almost two more weeks

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:03.803
to choose their next leader.

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:05.872
Officials have set a presidential run off

00:00:05.872 --> 00:00:07.707
on May 28, saying no candidate

00:00:07.707 --> 00:00:08.808
crossed the 50%

00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:11.177
threshold needed to win Sunday's vote.

00:00:11.511 --> 00:00:11.911
The two

00:00:11.911 --> 00:00:13.680
candidates headed to the final round

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.648
are incumbent Recep Tayyip Erdogan

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:17.584
and Kemal Klich, the Oracle. Mr.

00:00:17.584 --> 00:00:18.518
Erdogan's chief

00:00:18.518 --> 00:00:19.819
rival is an economist

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:20.954
backed by an alliance

00:00:20.954 --> 00:00:22.856
of several opposition parties.

00:00:22.856 --> 00:00:23.957
He is among those

00:00:23.957 --> 00:00:24.190
who say

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:25.692
the president is responsible

00:00:25.692 --> 00:00:27.794
for struggling economy.

00:00:27.794 --> 00:00:28.161
Mr.

00:00:28.161 --> 00:00:29.229
Erdogan's critics

00:00:29.229 --> 00:00:30.964
also blame him for a lackluster

00:00:30.964 --> 00:00:32.999
earthquake response that cost lives.

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:34.968
But he did better in the polls

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:36.236
than many expected.

00:00:36.236 --> 00:00:37.837
And his party is set to remain

00:00:37.837 --> 00:00:38.471
the largest

00:00:38.471 --> 00:00:41.074
in parliament Ahead of final results

00:00:41.074 --> 00:00:41.708
this morning.

00:00:41.708 --> 00:00:42.409
All this students

00:00:42.409 --> 00:00:43.643
Jomana Karadsheh joins me now

00:00:43.643 --> 00:00:45.278
live from Istanbul.

00:00:45.278 --> 00:00:46.246
And Jomana, it's

00:00:46.246 --> 00:00:48.448
not a win yet for Erdogan.

00:00:48.448 --> 00:00:48.882
Anything

00:00:48.882 --> 00:00:50.817
of course, is possible mathematically,

00:00:50.817 --> 00:00:52.152
but he's in a strong position

00:00:52.152 --> 00:00:53.019
ahead of this runoff.

00:00:53.019 --> 00:00:54.721
So what is your sense in the ground?

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:56.222
Is he likely

00:00:56.222 --> 00:00:57.791
to hold on to cling on to power here?

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:01.294
Well, I

00:01:01.294 --> 00:01:01.895
mean,

00:01:02.429 --> 00:01:03.229
you know,

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:05.532
so you have to look at the numbers. Yes.

00:01:05.532 --> 00:01:07.567
President Erdogan did not get that.

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:09.035
50 plus 1%

00:01:09.035 --> 00:01:11.237
that was needed to get the presidency.

00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:12.872
But he did do better than was

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:14.507
what was expected

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:16.476
in all the polling that was taking place

00:01:16.476 --> 00:01:18.344
before these elections.

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:20.380
They did have

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:22.215
calculated the role of the leader

00:01:22.215 --> 00:01:24.350
of the opposition in the lead.

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:25.185
And now you see that

00:01:25.185 --> 00:01:27.787
President Erdogan has pretty much

00:01:27.921 --> 00:01:30.924
come out with that slight lead

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:34.561
with more than 49% of the vote.

00:01:34.561 --> 00:01:36.029
And you've got both sides

00:01:36.029 --> 00:01:37.564
sounding very confident

00:01:37.564 --> 00:01:39.699
going into this second round.

00:01:39.699 --> 00:01:41.201
But a lot of the supporters

00:01:41.201 --> 00:01:43.369
of the opposition are very concerned

00:01:43.369 --> 00:01:44.871
that the opposition

00:01:44.871 --> 00:01:47.640
might not have that same determination

00:01:47.774 --> 00:01:49.809
in among its electorate,

00:01:49.809 --> 00:01:51.444
that same kind of enthusiasm.

00:01:51.444 --> 00:01:53.313
They went into that first round

00:01:53.313 --> 00:01:54.314
believing that

00:01:54.314 --> 00:01:56.015
that win from the first

00:01:56.015 --> 00:01:57.350
round was possible.

00:01:57.350 --> 00:02:00.753
Now you also have that third candidate

00:02:00.753 --> 00:02:01.688
who was running

00:02:01.688 --> 00:02:05.758
an ultra nationalist shenanigan

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:09.329
and he could potentially emerge from this

00:02:09.329 --> 00:02:13.199
as a tie breaker with those 5% votes.

00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:13.633
Of course, he's

00:02:13.633 --> 00:02:14.367
been eliminated

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:15.702
because only the top two

00:02:15.702 --> 00:02:17.704
will be headed towards that runoff

00:02:17.704 --> 00:02:20.573
and that 5% vote that

00:02:20.573 --> 00:02:23.977
he managed to garner in this election.

00:02:23.977 --> 00:02:25.411
What happens to that?

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:27.447
It is a combination of

00:02:27.981 --> 00:02:29.549
disenchanted nationalists

00:02:29.549 --> 00:02:30.550
who couldn't vote

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:33.386
for President Erdogan's alliance.

00:02:33.386 --> 00:02:33.720
And then

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:36.089
you've also got the protest voters

00:02:36.089 --> 00:02:37.891
who did not agree

00:02:37.891 --> 00:02:39.192
with the opposition's choice

00:02:39.192 --> 00:02:39.859
of came out cold,

00:02:39.859 --> 00:02:41.528
sterile or to

00:02:41.528 --> 00:02:42.862
to lead the opposition

00:02:42.862 --> 00:02:44.430
into these elections.

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:45.632
What happens to that?

00:02:45.632 --> 00:02:47.867
He spoke earlier to our colleague,

00:02:47.867 --> 00:02:49.002
Becky Anderson.

00:02:49.002 --> 00:02:50.937
Take a listen to what Sinan told her.

00:02:52.438 --> 00:02:53.606
What we're thinking is

00:02:53.606 --> 00:02:54.874
all the political parties

00:02:54.874 --> 00:02:57.076
should exclude terror organizations.

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:59.212
We don't have to give our support

00:02:59.212 --> 00:03:00.780
to either of the parties.

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:02.148
There is no such rule.

00:03:02.148 --> 00:03:03.683
When we first started this race,

00:03:03.683 --> 00:03:04.651
we thought we need to

00:03:04.651 --> 00:03:05.818
either win the government

00:03:05.818 --> 00:03:07.720
or we are going to be the kingmaker.

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:10.123
And we are at that status.

00:03:10.123 --> 00:03:12.458
Political parties like FDP or Huda.

00:03:12.859 --> 00:03:14.060
We want those candidates

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:15.395
not to rely on parties

00:03:15.395 --> 00:03:16.396
that have no distance

00:03:16.396 --> 00:03:17.764
between terrorist groups.

00:03:17.764 --> 00:03:20.233
And we succeeded in that

00:03:22.869 --> 00:03:25.371
And we're going to have to wait and see.

00:03:25.438 --> 00:03:26.806
Isa, he did say that

00:03:26.806 --> 00:03:28.575
he is going to be in consultations

00:03:28.575 --> 00:03:30.610
with the four other parties

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:32.178
that are part of his

00:03:32.178 --> 00:03:33.146
small alliance

00:03:33.146 --> 00:03:34.314
to see what they decide

00:03:34.314 --> 00:03:34.914
to do

00:03:34.914 --> 00:03:36.583
in the next couple of weeks,

00:03:36.583 --> 00:03:38.351
whether they're going to endorse anyone.

00:03:38.351 --> 00:03:39.686
But then there's also the question

00:03:39.686 --> 00:03:41.321
of those who voted for him.

00:03:41.321 --> 00:03:42.455
Will they be following

00:03:42.455 --> 00:03:43.990
whatever his decision is or will

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:46.192
they be going their own way?

00:03:46.192 --> 00:03:47.393
A critical couple of weeks

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:49.462
ahead for Turkey, ahead of a yet

00:03:49.462 --> 00:03:51.397
another consequential vote

00:03:51.397 --> 00:03:52.065
for this country

00:03:52.065 --> 00:03:53.266
that people would tell you

00:03:53.266 --> 00:03:54.968
is not just about the next five years,

00:03:54.968 --> 00:03:55.668
but the direction

00:03:55.668 --> 00:03:58.104
their country is taking. Indeed.

00:03:58.104 --> 00:04:00.540
And they're not giving much away,

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:02.008
very much playing the role

00:04:02.008 --> 00:04:03.643
potentially of kingmaker.

00:04:03.643 --> 00:04:04.410
But look, let's talk

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:06.512
about the opposition, because, of course,

00:04:06.512 --> 00:04:07.213
all the numbers

00:04:07.213 --> 00:04:08.615
we've been seeing ahead of this

00:04:08.615 --> 00:04:11.050
was that they're going to do fairly well.

00:04:11.317 --> 00:04:12.986
They now have two weeks now

00:04:12.986 --> 00:04:15.388
to wait for this runoff, Jomana.

00:04:15.388 --> 00:04:16.656
What is the mood right now?

00:04:16.656 --> 00:04:18.291
Do they fear they will lose momentum?

00:04:18.291 --> 00:04:19.959
Can they re-energize the

00:04:19.959 --> 00:04:21.661
population at this stage?

00:04:24.764 --> 00:04:26.065
That is going to be the question.

00:04:26.065 --> 00:04:27.634
That's going to be the big challenge

00:04:27.634 --> 00:04:30.570
because there was real disappointment

00:04:30.737 --> 00:04:33.172
among the voters for the opposition

00:04:33.172 --> 00:04:34.841
among their supporters.

00:04:34.841 --> 00:04:36.409
They really were expecting something

00:04:36.409 --> 00:04:37.243
very different.

00:04:37.243 --> 00:04:38.578
They believe that chemical it's

00:04:38.578 --> 00:04:40.513
the ruler in this alliance

00:04:40.513 --> 00:04:42.515
has underperformed.

00:04:42.515 --> 00:04:44.017
People really have their hope

00:04:44.017 --> 00:04:47.220
in this united front, this opposition

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:48.388
coming together in a way

00:04:48.388 --> 00:04:50.356
they have never done before.

00:04:50.356 --> 00:04:53.326
You've had these six diverse parties

00:04:53.993 --> 00:04:57.163
backed by the Kurds as well,

00:04:57.163 --> 00:04:58.231
all coming together

00:04:58.231 --> 00:04:59.432
as this one coalition.

00:04:59.432 --> 00:05:00.466
They were hoping to unseat

00:05:00.466 --> 00:05:01.367
President Erdogan.

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:04.237
Their promise was really speaking

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:07.173
to the disgruntlement

00:05:07.173 --> 00:05:08.775
of much of the population

00:05:08.775 --> 00:05:09.842
here, promising them

00:05:09.842 --> 00:05:11.010
change, promising

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:12.412
that real democracy

00:05:12.412 --> 00:05:14.414
under a parliamentary system

00:05:14.414 --> 00:05:17.317
will come back again under this

00:05:18.117 --> 00:05:20.753
this opposition if they do win.

00:05:20.753 --> 00:05:21.754
And there was this feeling

00:05:21.754 --> 00:05:23.289
that they could achieve this.

00:05:23.289 --> 00:05:24.357
They were promising that they could

00:05:24.357 --> 00:05:25.992
potentially do this from the first round.

00:05:25.992 --> 00:05:26.492
Then you had

00:05:26.492 --> 00:05:27.627
the polls that were coming out

00:05:27.627 --> 00:05:29.729
and putting chemical its true blue

00:05:29.729 --> 00:05:30.430
in the lead.

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:31.097
So right now

00:05:31.097 --> 00:05:32.999
you have the serious disappointment,

00:05:32.999 --> 00:05:34.067
but you're also hearing

00:05:34.067 --> 00:05:35.101
from the opposition

00:05:35.101 --> 00:05:36.069
saying that they are ready

00:05:36.069 --> 00:05:36.636
for this second

00:05:36.636 --> 00:05:38.204
round chemical solution, saying

00:05:38.204 --> 00:05:40.073
today he's not going anywhere.

00:05:40.073 --> 00:05:41.507
He is here in here to stay

00:05:41.507 --> 00:05:44.577
and he will fight until the last moment.

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:45.545
But we will have to see

00:05:45.545 --> 00:05:47.146
because I mean, you saw yesterday,

00:05:47.146 --> 00:05:48.581
we saw these incredible scenes

00:05:48.581 --> 00:05:51.017
where you had so many people turning out

00:05:51.684 --> 00:05:53.219
Turkey does have a history

00:05:53.219 --> 00:05:55.121
of high turnout at elections.

00:05:55.121 --> 00:05:56.756
Yesterday was a record turnout.

00:05:56.756 --> 00:05:59.158
Nearly 90% of eligible

00:05:59.158 --> 00:06:00.326
voters were out voting.

00:06:00.326 --> 00:06:03.730
We saw the elderly being brought

00:06:03.730 --> 00:06:05.164
into these polling centers

00:06:05.164 --> 00:06:06.933
on stretchers and on wheelchairs.

00:06:06.933 --> 00:06:08.434
We spoke to first time voters

00:06:08.434 --> 00:06:09.302
who were saying

00:06:09.302 --> 00:06:11.571
that this was the most decisive election

00:06:11.571 --> 00:06:13.873
in the history of their country.

00:06:13.873 --> 00:06:15.541
And they felt that they had an obligation

00:06:15.541 --> 00:06:16.309
to take part in that.

00:06:16.309 --> 00:06:17.977
And a lot of people that we spoke

00:06:17.977 --> 00:06:20.346
to were saying that they wanted change

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:21.814
But clearly,

00:06:21.814 --> 00:06:23.216
if you look at the results,

00:06:23.216 --> 00:06:26.119
you see a very divided Turkey.

00:06:26.152 --> 00:06:27.754
It is really a reflection

00:06:27.754 --> 00:06:30.223
of the state of polarization

00:06:30.223 --> 00:06:31.057
in this country.

00:06:31.057 --> 00:06:34.227
Two very different men, two very

00:06:34.861 --> 00:06:36.596
different visions

00:06:36.596 --> 00:06:38.030
for the future of the country.

00:06:38.030 --> 00:06:40.266
And Turks are very much divided

00:06:40.266 --> 00:06:41.134
on what Turkey

00:06:41.134 --> 00:06:43.436
they want to emerge out of this election.

00:06:43.436 --> 00:06:45.037
And then the work begins of

00:06:45.037 --> 00:06:46.739
how do you unite the country?

00:06:46.739 --> 00:06:47.240
Like you said,

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:49.108
Jomana, this clearly polarized.

00:06:49.108 --> 00:06:50.610
Jomana Karadsheh there for us.

00:06:50.610 --> 00:06:51.711
Thanks very much, Jomana.

